ame><surname>Minard</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Laicher</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Timchalk</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>3D 3He diffusion MRI as a local in vivo morphometric tool to evaluate emphysematous rat lungs.</article-title><source>J Appl Physiol</source></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0006670-Sato1"><label>31</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sato</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirai</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Imura</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kita</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Iwano</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Morphological mechanism of the development of pulmonary emphysema in klotho mice.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>104</volume><fpage>2361</fpage><lpage>2365</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17284608</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>This work was supported by Battelle Memorial Institute (<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.battelle.org">www.battelle.org</ext-link>) as part of a Pulmonary Systems Biology Initiative, a competitive internally funded program; the individuals making funding decisions had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript. This work was also supported by National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute (<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.nhlbi.nih.gov">www.nhlbi.nih.gov</ext-link>) Grant R01-HL-073598.</p></fn></fn-gro